# Codebase Knowledge Maintainer

Source code says **how**. The knowledge base says **what, why, and where**.

The knowledge base at `knowledge/` is a structured semantic map of the repository — not documentation, not a copy of source code. The source code is always the implementation authority.

---

## On Entry — Read State First

Before any task, read `knowledge/.state`:

```yaml
# knowledge/.state
bootstrap_complete: false
last_full_review: null
```

- `bootstrap_complete: false` → run bootstrapping phases before task work
- `bootstrap_complete: true` → proceed with targeted navigation and incremental updates

---

## Directory Structure

```
knowledge/
├── AGENTS.md        ← agent entry instructions
├── .state           ← bootstrap status
├── index.md         ← root map (start here)
├── architecture/    ← system structure, tech choices
├── features/        ← one subdirectory per feature
├── business/        ← cross-cutting business rules
├── flows/           ← end-to-end user flows
└── decisions/       ← architectural constraints not to violate
```

Navigate top-down from `knowledge/index.md`. Every directory with multiple concepts has an `index.md`.

---

## Three Levels

| Level | Examples | Answers |
|---|---|---|
| **Map** | `index.md`, `features/index.md` | What exists? Where do I look? |
| **Concept** | `features/chat/index.md`, `business/permissions.md` | What does this mean? What are the rules? |
| **Implementation** | `features/chat/realtime/implementation.md` | How exactly does this work? |

